/dev/v4l-subdev* 0660 root camera
# Hantro VPU register windows (uio0/1/2 = "pxa-hantro"; uio0 decoder, uio2 encoder).
# Group was "system" in 5.1, where the OMX components lived inside mediaserver (uid
# media) and owner-rw was enough. Android 7 split mediaserver up: OMX now runs in
# /system/bin/mediacodec as uid mediacodec, which is neither the owner nor in group
# system, so every hardware decode failed at
#   Hantro-DWL-lib: DWLReadAsicID: failed to open /dev/uio0
#   Hantro-DWL-lib: DWL: failed to get register base and size
#   Mrvl_MM: DecoderInitAlloc_Hantro() failed with error -9999
#   ACodec: ERROR(0x80001009)   <- OMX_ErrorHardware
# and playback died with MediaPlayer error(1, ...). Use group camera instead: it is
# mediacodec's primary gid AND a supplementary group of mediaserver, so both reach the
# VPU (matching how /dev/uio3 is already handed to the camera side). Owner stays media.
/dev/uio0 0660 media camera
/dev/uio1 0660 media camera
/dev/uio2 0660 media camera
/dev/ire 0660 root graphics
/dev/rfkill 0660 system wifi
/dev/tzdd 0660 system drmrpc
/dev/i2c-5 0660 media media
/sys/devices/virtual/input/input* active 0660 root input
/sys/devices/virtual/input/input* interval 0660 root input
/sys/devices/virtual/input/input* wake 0660 root input
/dev/input/event* 0660 system input
/dev/ttyACM* 0660 radio radio
/dev/ion 0666 system media
/dev/mbtchar* 0660 system net_bt_stack
/dev/st21nfca 0600 nfc nfc
/dev/ttyS0 0600 system system
/dev/alarm-poweroff 0660 system system
/dev/block/platform/soc.1/by-name/persistent 0600 system system

